    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d990-a5">

                <pb facs="0755" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg639"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]<anchor n="79" xml:id="d990-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-25T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of relations existing between this Government and the Huerta Government,
                    you and such members of your staff as are American citizens are directed to
                    leave your post at the earliest opportunity. Place consular offices and archives
                    with coats of arms, flags and seals in custody of the consular officer of Great
                    Britain and proceed to the United States or place of safety bringing code,
                    current accounts and fee stamps with you. Procure vouchers for transportation
                    expenses of your family. Naval vessel instructed to afford transportation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d990-f1" n="79" xml:id="d990-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Frontera.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
